WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.005
A default policy you can start with.

2
00:00:02.285 --> 00:00:10.243
Until your own measurements say otherwise: use the tool your team already has, configured well (weeks 2 and 3 matter more than switching).

3
00:00:10.523 --> 00:00:13.957
Leave the model and effort at their defaults for everyday work.

4
00:00:14.237 --> 00:00:20.851
Raise effort for bugs in unfamiliar code, intermittent failures, and changes that must find every usage.

5
00:00:21.131 --> 00:00:23.819
Lower it for fast, closely watched iteration.

6
00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:27.512
Route simple, repetitive subagent work to a small model.

7
00:00:27.792 --> 00:00:29.371
Watch /usage weekly.

8
00:00:29.651 --> 00:00:35.475
And whenever someone proposes a switch, ask for five tasks, three runs each, and cost per success.
